luence formula with leave-one-out leverage correction (Eq. infl) is the core of the studied configuration and the decisive B2 comparator, yet it is presented without any citation to influence-function or deletion-diagnostic literature. Only Broderick et al. is cited for data dropping.\",\n      \"anchor_text\": \"Deleting row $i$ perturbs the stationarity condition by $-\\\\nabla\\\\ell_i$, so a Newton step predicts the change of the gap\",\n      \"search_topics\": [\n        \"influence functions for understanding black-box predictions\",\n        \"Cook's distance case deletion influence logistic regression\",\n        \"one-step approximation leave-one-out for M-estimators\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_id\": \"manipulation-positioning\",\n      \"section\": \"Related Work\",\n      \"priority\": \"medium\",\n      \"citation_intent\": \"positioning\",\n      \"reason\": \"The 'Scope of the bibliography' paragraph and Extended limitations explicitly concede that work on adversarial manipulation of crowd-vote leaderboards is relevant but uncited, and the Introduction and Discussion motivate the budget through 'deliberate action' and rigging. One or two papers would let the paper position itself instead of disclaiming.\",\n      \"anchor_text\": \"Work on adversarial manipulation of crowd-vote leaderboards, on evaluation practices of arena-style platforms, and on influence functions\",\n      \"search_topics\": [\n        \"adversarial vote manipulation of LLM arena leaderboards\",\n        \"robustness of rankings from pairwise comparisons to adversarial or corrupted comparisons\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"failure_reason\": \"\"\n}\nEOF\ncat > draft_reference_gaps.md <<'EOF'\n# Draft reference gap analysis\n\n**Status:** ready. Three targeted retrieval targets.\n\nCoverage of Bradley–Terry theory (extensions, existence/consistency, uncertainty) is dense. The existing bibliography does not cover three areas the draft relies on or motivates itself with.